{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.OcneanuWeightTwoRowNonzero","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.OcneanuWeightTwoRowNonzero","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.OcneanuWeight"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuWeight_conventionD_ne_zero_of_two_rows","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuWeight_conventionD_ne_zero_of_two_rows","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeightTwoRowNonzero.lean#L107-L125","doc":"**The Ocneanu weight is nonzero on the at-most-two-row shapes** at convention\n`D`, under exactly the genericity `wtrace` already carries.\n\nComplementary to `ocneanuWeight_conventionD_eq_zero_of_three_rows`, and — see the\nmodule docstring — **not** conditional on Wenzl's theorem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.row_le_one_of_rowLen_two_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.row_le_one_of_rowLen_two_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeightTwoRowNonzero.lean#L99-L105","doc":"**At most two rows means every cell has `i ≤ 1`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuNumFactor_conventionD_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuNumFactor_conventionD_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeightTwoRowNonzero.lean#L79-L97","doc":"**The numerator factor is nonzero off content `−2`**, given `hgen`.\n\n`i ≤ j + 1` is what an at-most-two-row shape supplies (`i ≤ 1 ≤ j + 1`); it makes\nthe exponent gap `j + 2 - i` positive, and `hgen` does the rest. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuNumFactor_conventionD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuNumFactor_conventionD","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeightTwoRowNonzero.lean#L67-L77","doc":"**The numerator factor at convention `D`, in closed form.**\n\n`q² − 1 − q·z = −1/(q²+1)` at `z = q³/(q²+1)`, which collapses the two terms into\na single difference of powers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.hookLength_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.hookLength_pos","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeightTwoRowNonzero.lean#L56-L65","doc":"**A cell's hook length is positive** — its own arm contains it. ","signatureChunk":0}]}